# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw StatsBomb downloads (~320 MB) — regenerated by build_runs.py on first run
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/raw/

# Large intermediates. The files the app needs at runtime are committed
# explicitly (see the !negations below); everything else is rebuildable.
data/processed/*
!data/processed/runs.parquet
!data/processed/minutes.parquet
!data/processed/frames_app.parquet
!data/processed/threat_grid.npy

# Logs and scratch renders
outputs/*.log
outputs/figures/

# docs/ is personal reference and submission material, not repo content. The
# write-up is emailed as a PDF/DOCX; the book, technical report, one-pager and
# walkthrough notes are for my own prep. Several also quote figures that were
# later corrected (127 matches, +0.0178, +0.0071 -- the last being the
# mislabelled baseline whose CORRECTION is a headline point in AI_USAGE.md), so
# shipping them next to the write-up would contradict it. None are deliverables
# under §5 of the brief: code+README, the write-up, Part 2, the AI log, Part 3.
docs/

# The earlier markdown write-up. Superseded by the 3-page PDF/DOCX that is emailed,
# and it still quoted 127 matches, "85% usable" and +0.0071 -- the discredited
# figure. Two write-ups that disagree is worse than one. Kept on disk.
WRITEUP.md

# Personal preparation material — not part of the deliverable
walkthrough/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# OS / Office cruft
.DS_Store
._*
~$*
